course: dictionary
lesson: 8611
title: Many meanings of scratch
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, so you need the context to know which one the writer means. Look at the words around it. Ask what is happening, and what would make sense there.
explain: «Bubbles start at tiny places like scratches or specks.» Here a scratch is a thin mark on a surface, like a mark on glass. You can tell because the bubbles start at tiny places, and marks are places where bubbles can gather.
explain: «It's just a scratch» can be said by a friend who is hurt, scared or in trouble. They may be embarrassed, not want a fuss, or not want to get into trouble. The words around it show you that the hurt might be bigger than they are saying.
explain: When you are not sure, swap your meaning into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: To scratch is to rub your skin with your nails, usually because it itches.
fact: To scratch can also mean to make a mark or cut on a surface with something sharp or rough.
fact: A scratch is a thin mark or small cut.
fact: «From scratch» means from the very beginning, with nothing ready-made.
fact: «Old Scratch» (old-fashioned, US) means the Devil.
exercise: «Bubbles start at tiny places like scratches or specks.» In this sentence, scratch means | A loud song played at a party | *A thin mark on a surface | A type of bubble that pops quickly | A dance move
exercise: A friend says «It's just a scratch» after falling off a bike. What do they probably mean? | They want everyone to make a big fuss over them | *They are hurt, but they do not want a fuss | They are hungry and want lunch | They have a very deep wound that needs a doctor now
exercise: Which phrase means from the very beginning, with nothing ready-made? | *From scratch | Scratch out loud | Not up to scratch | Scratch your head
test: Why should you not scratch an insect bite? | *Scratching can make it worse and let germs in | Scratching makes the itch go away for ever | Scratching makes the bite smaller and drier | Scratching turns the bite into a bubble
test: Why might a cat scratch you? | *It was handled roughly | It wanted a new name | It was sleeping in the sun | It was fed a big dinner
exam: What does «Old Scratch» mean, according to the dictionary? | *The Devil | A very old cat | A kind old man | A scratchy old sweater
